<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#accountCurrency> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A currency or crypto asset that this financial account holds or is denominated in."@en .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#accountCurrency> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "accountCurrency"@en .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#accountCurrency> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Intentionally multi-valued: an account, including a hosted exchange account or multi-asset wallet, may hold or support more than one currency."@en .
# 
# https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#accountOf
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#accountOf> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#accountOf> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#Account> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#accountOf> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#Agent> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#accountOf> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The Agent that holds this Account, or to whom it is beneficially attributed. Inverse of stonework:hasAccount."@en .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#accountOf> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "accountOf" .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#accountOf> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "For a UserAccount this is the account holder; for a FinancialAccount it is the accountholder or beneficial owner, which may differ from whoever operates it (an account-takeover attacker operating a victim's FinancialAccount is modeled with stonework:controls from the attacker-held UserAccount, leaving accountOf pointing at the victim)."@en .
# 
# https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#actsOn
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#actsOn> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#actsOn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#CyberActivity> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#actsOn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#CyberEntity> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#actsOn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#used> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#actsOn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Links a CyberActivity to the CyberEntity it acted upon — the asset, artifact, or resource the activity operated against."@en .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#actsOn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "actsOn" .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#actsOn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Mirrors prov:used (an Activity used an Entity). Typical range instances are stonework:Host, stonework:RuntimeProcess, or other stonework:DigitalArtifact/stonework:Infrastructure individuals — e.g. the specific lsass.exe stonework:RuntimeProcess a credential-dumping attempt acted on. Distinct from stonework:targets: targets is a direct, open-domain/range lift of the STIX 2.1 relationship_type 'targets' shortcut, describing higher-level strategic targeting (a Sector, a Location, an Agent) by a Campaign/MalwareSample/ThreatActor. actsOn is purpose-built for the concrete technical asset one execution-trace Activity acted upon — the same distinction develop draws between stonework:mitigates (open, STIX-lifted) and stonework:mitigatesAttackPattern (purpose-built, controlled domain/range)."@en .
