# 
# https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#assertionObject
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#assertionObject> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#assertionObject> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#assertionObject> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#QualifiedAssertion> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#assertionObject> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Identifies the resource in the object or target position of a qualified assertion."@en .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#assertionObject> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "assertion object"@en .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#assertionObject> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Range is intentionally unset because framework relationships may target either a CyberEntity, a CyberActivity, or another externally defined resource."@en .
# 
# https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#assertionSubject
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#assertionSubject> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#assertionSubject> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#assertionSubject> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#QualifiedAssertion> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#assertionSubject> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Identifies the resource in the subject or source position of a qualified assertion."@en .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#assertionSubject> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "assertion subject"@en .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#assertionSubject> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Range is intentionally unset because framework relationships may originate from either a CyberEntity, a CyberActivity, or another externally defined resource."@en .
# 
# https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#assessmentOf
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#assessmentOf> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#assessmentOf> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#Assessment> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#assessmentOf> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Relates an Assessment to the entity being assessed."@en .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#assessmentOf> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "assessmentOf"@en .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#assessmentOf> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Scheme-specific linking properties, such as stonework:cvssMetricFor, are declared rdfs:subPropertyOf this property, so a query over assessmentOf reaches every Assessment subclass regardless of scheme."@en .
# 
# https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#assignedBy
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#assignedBy> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#assignedBy> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#assignedBy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#Vulnerability> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#assignedBy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#Agent> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#assignedBy> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Relates a vulnerability to the numbering authority that assigned its primary vulnerability identifier."@en .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#assignedBy> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "assignedBy"@en .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#assignedBy> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Resolve source-native names, UUIDs, or email addresses to an Agent individual. Like stonework:vulnerabilityId and stonework:dateAssigned, this property describes the vulnerability record's single primary identifier; represent independently assigned identifiers as distinct vulnerability records. The unresolved source string is preserved separately on cve:assigner regardless of whether resolution succeeds."@en .
# 
# https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#assignedRole
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#assignedRole> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#assignedRole> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#assignedRole> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#RoleAssignment> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#assignedRole> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#Role> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#assignedRole> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The Role assigned by a qualified RoleAssignment."@en .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#assignedRole> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "assignedRole"@en .
# 
# https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#associatedWith
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#associatedWith> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#associatedWith> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Generic association between two entities. Use a more specific property where one exists."@en .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#associatedWith> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "associatedWith" .
# 
# https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#attributedTo
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#attributedTo> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#attributedTo> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Links a CyberActivity to the Agent responsible for, or associated with, performing it." .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#attributedTo> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "attributedTo" .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#attributedTo> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Domain/range intentionally left unset: this property is a direct lift of the STIX 2.1 relationship_type 'attributed-to' shortcut. STIX does not schema-constrain which SDO/SCO types may appear as source_ref/target_ref for a given relationship_type — that's producer convention, not enforceable structure, and a closed domain/range here would misrepresent real STIX 2.1 data and mislead reasoner-based consumers. In practice the object is typically a stonework:Agent — most often a stonework:ThreatActor in the adversarial case, matching STIX's own convention for 'attributed-to' — but stonework:CyberActivity is a general occurrence class covering defensive and neutral activities too (Investigations, a ControlPlan's Process), so the performer need not be adversarial."@en .
# 
# https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#attributedToAgent
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#attributedToAgent> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#attributedToAgent> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#DigitalIdentity> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#attributedToAgent> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#Agent> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#attributedToAgent> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Links a digital identity to the real-world Agent it is believed to belong to." .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#attributedToAgent> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "attributedToAgent" .
# 
# https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#authoredBy
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#authoredBy> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#authoredBy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#Provenance> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#authoredBy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#Agent> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#authoredBy> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The Agent who authored or produced this provenance record, source document, or intelligence artifact."@en .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#authoredBy> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "authoredBy"@en .
# 
# https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#beneficiaryAccount
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#beneficiaryAccount> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#beneficiaryAccount> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#FinancialTransaction> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#beneficiaryAccount> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#FinancialAccount> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#beneficiaryAccount> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The account credited by this transaction — the destination of the transferred value."@en .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#beneficiaryAccount> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "beneficiaryAccount"@en .
# 
# https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#beneficiaryMonetaryValue
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#beneficiaryMonetaryValue> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#beneficiaryMonetaryValue> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subPropertyOf> <https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#hasMonetaryValue> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#beneficiaryMonetaryValue> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#FinancialTransaction> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#beneficiaryMonetaryValue> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#MonetaryAmount> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#beneficiaryMonetaryValue> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The monetary amount credited to the beneficiary account as this transaction's output."@en .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#beneficiaryMonetaryValue> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "beneficiaryMonetaryValue"@en .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#beneficiaryMonetaryValue> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use with stonework:originatorMonetaryValue when a transaction changes denomination, as in a currency exchange. Both properties remain queryable through their stonework:hasMonetaryValue superproperty."@en .
# 
# https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#boundTo
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#boundTo> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#boundTo> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#boundTo> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#Variable> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#boundTo> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Thing> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#boundTo> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Binds a Variable, at execution time, to the individual it actually resolved to — e.g. the specific SecurityCondition instance a successful attempt produced."@en .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#boundTo> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "boundTo" .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#boundTo> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Used when the bound value is an instance of a class rather than a scalar; see stonework:boundToLiteral for scalar bindings. Tested by stonework:guardType on a Transition."@en .
# 
# https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#categorizedBy
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#categorizedBy> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#categorizedBy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#Category> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#categorizedBy> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Links any individual to one or more contextual categories." .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#categorizedBy> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "categorizedBy" .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#categorizedBy> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "This is the primary mechanism for flexible, context-sensitive classification (e.g., Evidence, HighValue, Suspect, etc.). Multiple categories per individual are allowed."@en .
