# 
# https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#controls
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#controls> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#controls> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#UserAccount> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#controls> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#FinancialAccount> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#controls> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A stonework:FinancialAccount that this stonework:UserAccount, a login or credential, can operate."@en .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#controls> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "controls"@en .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#controls> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Distinct from stonework:accountOf, which records the holder or beneficial owner. One login often controls several financial accounts; a financial account seen in isolation, such as an IBAN in wire data, may have no associated login. An account-takeover attacker holding a victim's UserAccount controls the victim's FinancialAccount without being its accountOf."@en .
# 
# https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#correspondsToStep
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#correspondsToStep> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#correspondsToStep> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#correspondsToStep> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#CyberActivity> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#correspondsToStep> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#Step> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#correspondsToStep> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso> <http://purl.org/net/p-plan#correspondsToStep> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#correspondsToStep> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Links an executing CyberActivity to the Step it is the concrete performance of."@en .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#correspondsToStep> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "correspondsToStep" .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#correspondsToStep> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Directly mirrors p-plan:correspondsToStep (domain prov:Activity, range p-plan:Step), narrowed to stonework:CyberActivity/stonework:Step. Declared functional, matching p-plan: a single CyberActivity corresponds to at most one Step, but a Step may still be the target of many CyberActivity instances across retries or repeated executions. Fills the gap noted on stonework:Step: the property linking an executing Activity back to the Step it realizes."@en .
