<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#executedOn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#RuntimeProcess> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#executedOn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#Host> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#executedOn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Relates a RuntimeProcess to the Host it ran on."@en .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#executedOn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "executedOn"@en .
# 
# https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#executionOf
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#executionOf> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#executionOf> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#inverseOf> <https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#hasExecution> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#executionOf> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#CyberActivity> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#executionOf> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#Behavior> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#executionOf> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Relates a CyberActivity to the Behavior plan whose execution it represents."@en .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#executionOf> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "executionOf"@en .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#executionOf> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Links an overall execution to the Behavior it carries out. This may be a full plan — an Investigation to an InvestigationPlan, an Operation to an OperationPlan, a Process to a Playbook or ControlPlan — or, in the lightweight case, a bare method: a CyberActivity may point directly at the stonework:Technique (or stonework:AttackTechnique) it performs, with no intervening Procedure, Plan, or Step. The lightweight form is the common one for sightings and incident timelines ('actor performed T1003.001 against this host at this time'); it can be elaborated into a Step-decomposed Plan later without changing the executionOf assertion. Use stonework:correspondsToStep for the finer-grained link between an executing CyberActivity and an individual Step when a Plan is present."@en .
# 
# https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#exploits
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#exploits> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#exploits> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Shortcut triple: source Malware or ThreatActor exploits target Vulnerability. Corresponds to STIX relationship_type 'exploits'." .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#exploits> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "exploits" .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#exploits> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Domain/range intentionally left unset: this property is a direct lift of the STIX 2.1 relationship_type 'exploits' shortcut. STIX does not schema-constrain which SDO/SCO types may appear as source_ref/target_ref for a given relationship_type — that's producer convention, not enforceable structure, and a closed domain/range here would misrepresent real STIX 2.1 data and mislead reasoner-based consumers."@en .
# 
# https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#exploitsWeakness
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#exploitsWeakness> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#exploitsWeakness> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subPropertyOf> <https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#hasWeakness> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#exploitsWeakness> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#Vulnerability> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#exploitsWeakness> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#Weakness> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#exploitsWeakness> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Relates a vulnerability to the weakness class it instantiates or exploits. Subproperty of stonework:hasWeakness, using the directional 'exploits' semantics aligned with CVE and CWE mapping conventions."@en .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#exploitsWeakness> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "exploitsWeakness"@en .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#exploitsWeakness> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "The range is a stonework:Weakness individual whose IRI is derived from the CWE identifier. Used by cve:exploitsWeakness (rdfs:subPropertyOf this property) when CVE data is loaded; query this property directly for cross-source lookups."@en .
# 
# https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#exposesService
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#exposesService> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#exposesService> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#Host> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#exposesService> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#NetworkService> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#exposesService> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Relates a Host to the NetworkServices it provides."@en .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#exposesService> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "exposesService"@en .
# 
# https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#fixedInProduct
