# 
# https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#inBlock
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#inBlock> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#inBlock> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#IPAddress> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#inBlock> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#IPBlock> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#inBlock> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Relates an IPAddress to the IPBlock whose address space contains it."@en .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#inBlock> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "inBlock"@en .
# 
# https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#indicates
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#indicates> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#indicates> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#Indicator> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#indicates> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Asserts that when the source Indicator's pattern is matched, it signals the presence of the target adversary behavior, malware, campaign, or threat actor." .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#indicates> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "indicates"@en .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#indicates> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Corresponds to STIX relationship_type 'indicates'. Domain is stonework:Indicator — unlike the source side of other STIX relationship shortcuts, this is definitional rather than open-world convention: an object is only ever an Indicator because it indicates something, per STIX's own spec role for that object type. Range is intentionally left unset: an Indicator may indicate all sorts of things (AttackPattern/AttackTechnique, Malware, Campaign, CyberActivityCluster, ThreatActor, Infrastructure, Tool, and whatever else a producer's pattern targets), and STIX does not schema-constrain the target_ref type for a given relationship_type. A single Indicator may indicate multiple targets."@en .
# 
# https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#initiatedBy
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#initiatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#initiatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#NetworkTraffic> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#initiatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#RuntimeProcess> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#initiatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The RuntimeProcess that opened this NetworkTraffic flow. Core process-to-network correlation arc for host-based forensics and lateral movement analysis."@en .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#initiatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "initiatedBy"@en .
# 
# https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#installationOf
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#installationOf> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#installationOf> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#VersionedProduct> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#installationOf> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Relates a component context to the versioned product it references or instantiates."@en .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#installationOf> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "installation of" .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#installationOf> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Used by stonework:BomEntry (declarative — a component listed in an SBOM), stonework:ProductInstallation (observational — a verified deployment on a specific system), and other stonework:ComponentContext subclasses. Domain is intentionally left unset to avoid restricting future component-context subclasses. Not declared owl:FunctionalProperty at the property level, because not every ComponentContext subclass is one-to-one with a product — a source-native advisory entry may legitimately name several. BomEntry and ProductInstallation instead carry a local owl:maxQualifiedCardinality 1 restriction on this property (onClass stonework:VersionedProduct), which gives those two classes the same at-most-one guarantee without constraining subclasses that don't share it."@en .
# 
# https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#installedOn
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#installedOn> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#installedOn> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#inverseOf> <https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#hasProductInstallation> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#installedOn> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#installedOn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#ProductInstallation> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#installedOn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#Infrastructure> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#installedOn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Relates a ProductInstallation to the Infrastructure entity on which that product instance is installed."@en .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#installedOn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "installedOn"@en .
# 
# https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#intermediaryAccount
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#intermediaryAccount> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#intermediaryAccount> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#FinancialTransaction> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#intermediaryAccount> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#FinancialAccount> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#intermediaryAccount> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A correspondent or intermediary account through which this transaction is routed between originator and beneficiary."@en .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#intermediaryAccount> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "intermediaryAccount"@en .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#intermediaryAccount> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Multi-valued and unordered in this revision; a strict correspondent-banking chain order is deferred."@en .
