<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#locatedWithin> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#Location> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#locatedWithin> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Relates a Location to a broader Location that wholly contains it, e.g. a City to its Region or Country, or a Region to its Country."@en .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#locatedWithin> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "locatedWithin"@en .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#locatedWithin> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Transitive: a City locatedWithin a Region that is locatedWithin a Country is also locatedWithin that Country. Assert only the most direct containment and let reasoning supply the rest. Use stonework:locatedAt to place non-Location entities such as Hosts or Organizations at a Location."@en .
