# 
# https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#mitigates
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#mitigates> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#mitigates> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Relates a Mitigation, CourseOfAction, or Control to the AttackPattern or Vulnerability it addresses. Corresponds to STIX relationship_type 'mitigates'."@en .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#mitigates> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "mitigates" .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#mitigates> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Domain/range intentionally left unset: this property is a direct lift of the STIX 2.1 relationship_type 'mitigates' shortcut. STIX does not schema-constrain which SDO/SCO types may appear as source_ref/target_ref for a given relationship_type — that's producer convention, not enforceable structure, and a closed domain/range here would misrepresent real STIX 2.1 data and mislead reasoner-based consumers. Contrast with stonework:mitigatesAttackPattern, a purpose-built subproperty with a controlled domain/range, populated by materialize-technique-links.sparql rather than lifted directly from STIX."@en .
# 
# https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#mitigatesAttackPattern
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#mitigatesAttackPattern> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#mitigatesAttackPattern> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subPropertyOf> <https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#mitigates> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#mitigatesAttackPattern> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#Countermeasure> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#mitigatesAttackPattern> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#AttackPattern> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#mitigatesAttackPattern> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Relates a Countermeasure (e.g. a CIS Control safeguard) to the AttackPattern it mitigates, resolved from a shared technique identifier."@en .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#mitigatesAttackPattern> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "mitigatesAttackPattern" .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#mitigatesAttackPattern> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Materialized by joining a framework's technique-identifier literal (see stonework:relatedTechniqueIdentifier, e.g. cis:mitigatesTechniqueId) against the ATT&CK technique's external reference. Framework ontologies declare their concrete property (e.g. cis:mitigatesTechnique) as rdfs:subPropertyOf this."@en .
# 
# https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#mitigatesVulnerability
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#mitigatesVulnerability> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#mitigatesVulnerability> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#CourseOfAction> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#mitigatesVulnerability> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#Vulnerability> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#mitigatesVulnerability> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A CourseOfAction (patch, workaround, compensating control) addresses this Vulnerability. Distinct from stonework:mitigates (Countermeasure → AttackPattern)."@en .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#mitigatesVulnerability> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "mitigatesVulnerability"@en .
# 
