<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#observedIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#CyberActivity> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#observedIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Relates an observed entity, such as a DigitalArtifact, Infrastructure, Malware, Product, Behavior, Identifier, or SecurityCondition, to the CyberActivity (for example a Campaign, Incident, or Event) in which it was observed or collected."@en .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#observedIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "observedIn"@en .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#observedIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "A general-purpose shortcut: the kind of context is conveyed by typing the CyberActivity, so narrower subproperties per activity type are unnecessary. Asserting this property does not imply that the object is a Campaign; type it explicitly when that matters. When an observation needs its own metadata, such as observer, time, location, count, or confidence, model it as a stonework:Sighting instead. Not an inverse of stonework:uses, which records that an actor, campaign, or malware employs a technique or tool rather than that an entity was seen in an activity."@en .
