# 
# https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#precededByStep
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#precededByStep> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#precededByStep> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#Step> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#precededByStep> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#Step> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#precededByStep> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Relates a Step to another Step that must occur before it within the same parent Behavior."@en .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#precededByStep> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "precededByStep" .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#precededByStep> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Deliberately distinct from stonework:precedes, whose domain and range are IntelligenceProduct (report-version succession) — an unrelated relationship. precededByStep expresses a graph that may contain cycles: an edge targeting an already-reached Step is a loop, not an error. Use stonework:Transition instead when the edge itself needs a guard condition or other structure attached."@en .
# 
# https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#precedes
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#precedes> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#precedes> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#IntelligenceProduct> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#precedes> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#IntelligenceProduct> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#precedes> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Temporal succession of Information (v1 precedes v2 of a report)"@en .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#precedes> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "precedes" .
# 
# https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#predictedType
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#predictedType> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#predictedType> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#predictedType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#Hypothesis> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#predictedType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Class> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#predictedType> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The class a Hypothesis predicts its stonework:predictsVariable will be bound to an instance of, once executed."@en .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#predictedType> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "predictedType" .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#predictedType> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Mirrors stonework:guardType on Transition. Exists because a Hypothesis is typically formed before the Variable's eventual value has been constructed — at prediction time there is usually no individual yet to name via stonework:predictedValue, only an expected class of outcome (e.g. 'this attempt will produce some stonework:SecurityCondition')."@en .
# 
# https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#predictedValue
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#predictedValue> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#predictedValue> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#predictedValue> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#Hypothesis> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#predictedValue> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Thing> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#predictedValue> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The individual a Hypothesis predicts its stonework:predictsVariable will be bound to, once executed."@en .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#predictedValue> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "predictedValue" .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#predictedValue> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Mirrors stonework:boundTo on the actual-result side; usable only when a specific pre-existing individual is predicted. See stonework:predictedType for the more common case of predicting a class of outcome rather than a specific not-yet-constructed individual, and stonework:predictedLiteral for predictions of a scalar."@en .
# 
# https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#predictsVariable
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#predictsVariable> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#predictsVariable> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#predictsVariable> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#Hypothesis> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#predictsVariable> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#Variable> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#predictsVariable> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The Variable whose eventual binding a Hypothesis is a prediction about."@en .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#predictsVariable> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "predictsVariable" .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#predictsVariable> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Because stonework:hasInputVariable/stonework:hasOutputVariable are declared on stonework:Behavior, and stonework:Step is itself a Behavior, a Hypothesis may predict a Variable declared at any level of a Step/Plan decomposition — a top-level Plan's overall outcome or a single Step's individual result — without a separate property per level."@en .
# 
