# 
# https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#relatedAttackPattern
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#relatedAttackPattern> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#relatedAttackPattern> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#AttackPattern> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#relatedAttackPattern> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Relates an entity to an AttackPattern representing the same underlying technique in a different framework shape, resolved from a shared technique identifier (e.g. a CAPEC entry and the MITRE ATT&CK technique it maps to, or a CWE weakness and the CAPEC pattern that exploits it)."@en .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#relatedAttackPattern> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "relatedAttackPattern" .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#relatedAttackPattern> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Domain intentionally left unset: subjects include stonework:Weakness (CWE → CAPEC) and stonework:AttackPattern itself (CAPEC → ATT&CK). Materialized by joining a framework's technique-identifier literal (see stonework:relatedTechniqueIdentifier) against the ATT&CK technique's external reference. Framework ontologies declare their concrete property (e.g. capec:relatedAttackTechnique, cwe:relatedAttackPattern) as rdfs:subPropertyOf this."@en .
# 
# https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#relatedTechnique
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#relatedTechnique> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#relatedTechnique> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#CyberTechnique> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#relatedTechnique> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#CyberTechnique> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#relatedTechnique> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Relates a CyberTechnique to another related CyberTechnique via a cross-framework or cross-abstraction-level association."@en .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#relatedTechnique> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "relatedTechnique" .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#relatedTechnique> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "For technique-to-technique associations where both ends are already stonework:CyberTechnique individuals. Where the association instead crosses AttackPattern shapes (e.g. CWE weakness → CAPEC pattern, CAPEC pattern → ATT&CK technique), use stonework:relatedAttackPattern, whose domain is not restricted to CyberTechnique."@en .
