# 
# https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#supersededBy
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#supersededBy> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#supersededBy> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#TransitiveProperty> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#supersededBy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#Vulnerability> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#supersededBy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#Vulnerability> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#supersededBy> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Relates a vulnerability to the vulnerability record that supersedes it, e.g. when a CVE is split, merged, or formally replaced by another identifier."@en .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#supersededBy> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "supersededBy"@en .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#supersededBy> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Corresponds to cve:replacedBy in CVE JSON 5.x, but as an object property linking to a stonework:Vulnerability individual rather than a string. The source-specific string form is preserved on cve:replacedBy regardless of whether resolution to this property succeeds."@en .
# 
# https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#supersedes
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#supersedes> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#supersedes> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#TransitiveProperty> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#supersedes> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#VersionedProduct> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#supersedes> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#VersionedProduct> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#supersedes> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Relates a product version to an older version it replaces. Transitive to support full product lifecycle reasoning."@en .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#supersedes> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "supersedes"@en .
# 
# https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#targets
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#targets> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#targets> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Shortcut triple: source targets the target Identity, Vulnerability, or Location. Corresponds to STIX relationship_type 'targets'." .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#targets> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "targets" .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#targets> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Domain/range intentionally left unset: this property is a direct lift of the STIX 2.1 relationship_type 'targets' shortcut. STIX does not schema-constrain which SDO/SCO types may appear as source_ref/target_ref for a given relationship_type — that's producer convention, not enforceable structure, and a closed domain/range here would misrepresent real STIX 2.1 data and mislead reasoner-based consumers."@en .
# 
# https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#targetsPlatform
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#targetsPlatform> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#targetsPlatform> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#VersionedProduct> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#targetsPlatform> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A MalwareSample or Tool is engineered to run on or exploit this VersionedProduct (OS, application, firmware version). Supports exposure and blast-radius queries."@en .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#targetsPlatform> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "targetsPlatform"@en .
# 
# https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#targetsService
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#targetsService> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
