<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#targetsService> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#NetworkService> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#targetsService> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The NetworkService this traffic addresses."@en .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#targetsService> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "targetsService"@en .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#targetsService> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "⚑ Category: service *type* (HTTP, SSH, RDP, SMB, DNS) is better expressed as stonework:categorizedBy → Category named individual than as subclasses of NetworkService. NetworkService as a class is appropriate only when the instance has its own properties (port, vulnerability linkage)." .
