# 
# https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#uses
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#uses> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#uses> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Relates a threat actor group, campaign, malware, or tool to an offensive technique, malware, or tool it is known to employ." .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#uses> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "uses" .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#uses> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Domain/range intentionally left unset: this property is a direct lift of the STIX 2.1 relationship_type 'uses' shortcut (sub-property stones:uses carries the shortcut triples emitted by the STIX 2.1 transform). STIX does not schema-constrain which SDO/SCO types may appear as source_ref/target_ref for a given relationship_type — that's producer convention, not enforceable structure. In the MITRE ATT&CK bundle alone, observed 'uses' sources include Campaign, IntrusionSet, Malware, and Tool, and observed targets include AttackTechnique, Malware, and Tool — a closed domain/range would misrepresent this real data and mislead reasoner-based consumers. Query-time discrimination (e.g. selecting only IntrusionSet users of a technique) should filter on the asserted stones:stixType literal or a specific rdf:type, not assume it from this property alone."@en .
