<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#attackId> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#attackId> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subPropertyOf> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#attackId> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#attackId> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The MITRE ATT&CK identifier of an ATT&CK object, as ATT&CK displays it: Txxxx or Txxxx.yyy (technique, sub-technique), TAxxxx (tactic), Gxxxx (group), Sxxxx (software), Mxxxx (mitigation), Cxxxx (campaign), DETxxxx (detection strategy), ANxxxx (analytic), DCxxxx (data component)."@en .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#attackId> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "attackId"@en .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#attackId> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Domain deliberately unset: every kind of ATT&CK object has an ATT&CK ID. The canonical and source forms are the same, so attack:attackId specializes both this property and stonework:externalId. Not unique across object types (ATT&CK's deprecated mitigations reuse technique T-numbers): look an object up by its ID together with its class. Distinct from stonework:relatedTechniqueIdentifier, which carries an ATT&CK technique ID on another framework's entity (e.g. a CAPEC pattern) as a join key; attackId is the ATT&CK object's own identifier."@en .
# 
# https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#bic
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#bic> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#bic> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#bic> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#FinancialInstitution> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#bic> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#bic> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The Business Identifier Code (SWIFT/BIC, ISO 9362) of this institution."@en .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#bic> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "bic"@en .
# 
# https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#blockchainNetwork
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#blockchainNetwork> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#blockchainNetwork> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#CryptoAsset> .
