<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#boundToLiteral> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Literal> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#boundToLiteral> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Binds a Variable, at execution time or at plan instantiation, to a scalar result value such as a boolean, count, or numeric score."@en .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#boundToLiteral> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "boundToLiteral" .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#boundToLiteral> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Tested by stonework:guardLiteralValue and stonework:guardOperator on a Transition. When the guard uses an ordering operator (LessThan, GreaterThanOrEqual, etc.), this value MUST carry a numeric datatype (xsd:decimal, xsd:double, or xsd:integer) — untyped or string literals do not compare numerically under SPARQL."@en .
