<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#locationPrecision> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The radius, in meters, of uncertainty around this Location's stonework:latitude and stonework:longitude."@en .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#locationPrecision> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "locationPrecision"@en .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#locationPrecision> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Corresponds to the STIX 2.1 Location precision property. Use it to distinguish an exact facility coordinate from a city- or region-level centroid, such as a geolocated IP address or an event geotagged from a news report. Omit it when the precision is unknown."@en .
