# https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#relatedTechniqueIdentifier
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#relatedTechniqueIdentifier> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#relatedTechniqueIdentifier> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#relatedTechniqueIdentifier> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A framework-native technique identifier string (e.g. a MITRE ATT&CK technique ID such as 'T1003.001') carried on an entity from another framework, both for provenance and as the join key used to materialize the corresponding stonework:relatedAttackPattern or stonework:mitigatesAttackPattern edge."@en .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#relatedTechniqueIdentifier> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "relatedTechniqueIdentifier" .
<https://cyberterrain.org/ns/stonework#relatedTechniqueIdentifier> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Domain intentionally left unset: populated on entities as different as capec:AttackPattern and cis:Control. Framework-specific subproperties (e.g. capec:attackTechniqueId, cis:mitigatesTechniqueId) carry the concrete literal. Retained after materialization — it records the source string as ingested, distinct from the resolved object-property edge."@en .
